 #uuid "326e15b0-6aef-59e0-9f84-d0b719d881bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-140318" :question/problem "Rewrite $-({x}^{2}+4x-12)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+4x-12\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x-12\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${2}^{2},$ writing the constant term $12$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}}_{⏟}-{2}^{2}-12\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}-{2}^{2}-12\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}-16.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({x}^{2}+4x-12) & =-({(x+2)}^{2}-16) \\\\  & =-{(x+2)}^{2}+16 \\\\  & =16-(x+2)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140318/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "808c9f7b-b951-5306-bce8-efc1aec8c2b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140318"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-218604/field-1/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "ed6b0261-a846-57d5-a14f-22443f707546" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218604/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "73cbe1d4-7fc7-5344-8de1-50283dc3c1fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218604/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd642314-3834-5f39-8342-90afb652d714" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218604/field-1/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer-field/choices ["q-218604/field-1/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc62