x+1$ by completing the square.\n\n$-{x}^{2}+16x+1=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-(x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$)^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({x}^{2}-16x-1)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-16x-1\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 8x-1\n$$\n\nThen, we add and then subtract ${8}^{2},$ writing the constant term $1$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 8x+{8}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{8}^{2}-1\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-8)^{2}-{8}^{2}-1\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-8)^{2}-65.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+16x+1 & =-((x-8)^{2}-65) \\\\  & =-(x-8)^{2}+65 \\\\  & =65-(x-8)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-218662/field-1" "q-218662/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "808c9f7b-b951-5306-bce8-efc1aec8c2b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-218662"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140321/selection/bc01296d596aa4fdee0ddd823e1b7b99ef43c444cde6b8f0c0f88ac4d312cbbc" :answer/id #uuid "66263f55-7671-54c7-b9de-dda2ebe88ab9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15-(y-5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140321/selection/f6d5cf2312884642ff82c3bd6ea8e08e12fa34a880c6d1cba77fc80f1d911405" :answer/id #uuid "2ab200dd-8e7a-5b3e-88a0-e2d99dbf810f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25-(y+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140321/selection/0addf87e1c45493b3a6dd4058927bdff84c7149919c5f7574624d57c5553aebb" :answer/id #uuid "92324395-65e2-5074-9ab3-d1fed5aad71c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10-(y-5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140321/selection/d96c5bca5f141e5e125f8d4deea8c7b9aac46bd560a30988dc6f47c7f8c66a9f" :answer/id #uuid "e6647176-4edb-5bce-b395-f92cac060123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5-(y+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140321/selection/ed37f07e8a366654d7a049795b7d940b77b417f42bcc36c6cb8561d3a75086f4" :answer/id #uuid "b2150979-7908-5780-8d5c-d9bfdd7b97f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-20-(y+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140321/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f9e4be2-2c71-59ac-894a-bdb97a475a30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140321/selection/d96c5bca5f141e5e125f8d4deea8c7b9aac46bd560a30988dc6f47c7f8c66a9f" :answer-field/choices ["q-140321/selection/bc01296d596aa4fdee0ddd823e1b7b99ef43c444cde6b8f0c0f88ac4d312cbbc" "q-140321/selection/f6d5cf2312884642ff82c3bd6ea8e08e12fa34a880c6d1cba77fc80f1d911405" "q-140321/selection/0addf87e1c45493b3a6dd4058927bdff84c7149919c5f7574624d57c5553aebb" "q-140321/selection/d96c5bca5f141e5e125f8d4deea8c7b9aac46bd560a30988dc6f47c7f8c66a9f" "q-140321/selection/ed37f07e8a366654d7a049795b7d940b77b417f42bcc36c6cb8561d3a75086f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140321" :question/id #uuid "56ba52e8-220b-5a72-98e6-d401a8d1bea8" :question/math-academy-id "q-140321" :question/problem "Rewrite $-({y}^{2}+10y+20)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+10y+20\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 5y+20\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $20$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}}_{⏟}-{5}^{2}+20\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y+5)^{2}-{5}^{2}+20\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y+5)^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({y}^{2}+5y+20) & =-({(y+5)}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =-{(y+5)}^{2}+5 \\\\  & =5-(y+5)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140321/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "808c9f7b-b951-5306-bce8-efc1aec8c2b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140410/selection/6cb3d6d8fd2979bc433a5f74c59630fdfb8d806264498190dae990818464c900" :answer/id #uuid "d7fb0fea-ccc4-560c-9e56-e17b25a805cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}+{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140410/selection/dd21ae001e09dbe0b1909a63227a046a693e8231e15742d4699cd175da2c087c" :answer/id #uuid "6795e805-f52f-52f9-8a77-4433c1c2094c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{45}{4}-{(y-10)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140410/selection/b45123bb727cca210ad649ed53454fdcf53a18bcb497aa75a278eabfaeb5de24" :answer/id #uuid "70890d95-d92c-51c4-a34f-beba51f6cfe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140410/selection/20399429aa0b136893fc25052c38fd5f9a385fc522d9b6aac30549ea94a5430e" :answer/id #uuid "3abf4b3e-07c9-56e6-963d-d65706ac1ef6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20-{(y-10)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140410/selection/1850eab6c908ad22c4fd3a33a02b57ebc7c473ae88bfe6b84f0d3ba1dcf8c2cd" :answer/id #uuid "b3bd5b3b-06bc-551f-a1c0-f7c93726986c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140410/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "72abfaf0-7e16-5881-80e5-4fb469833fbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140410/selection/b45123bb727cca210ad649ed53454fdcf53a18bcb497aa75a278eabfaeb5de24" :answer-field/choices ["q-140410/selection/6cb3d6d8fd2979bc433a5f74c59630fdfb8d806264498190dae990818464c900" "q-140410/selection/dd21ae001e09dbe0b1909a63227a046a693e8231e15742d4699cd175da2c087c" "q-140410/selection/b45123bb727cca210ad649ed53454fdcf53a18bcb497aa75a278eabfaeb5de24" "q-140410/selection/20399429aa0b136893fc25052c38fd5f9a385fc522d9b6aac30549ea94a5430e" "q-140410/selection/1850eab6c908ad22c4fd3a33a02b57ebc7c473ae88bfe6b84f0d3ba1dcf8c2cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140410" :question/id #uuid "80cdca89-f786-5241-acc4-7042ca73b8c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-140410" :question/problem "Rewrite $-{y}^{2}+5y-5$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({y}^{2}-5y+5)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-5y+5\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+5\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $5$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}+5y-5 & =-({(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140410/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a85fece-e40f-543c-b3c3-ae43a5175808"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14