 product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}x+10\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $10$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}x+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({x}^{2}+7x+10) & =-({(x+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(x+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}-{(x+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140330/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a85fece-e40f-543c-b3c3-ae43a5175808"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140337/selection/37f89d1418650fbe3501526df2d2242bbe0830d3026a8506f8c50efdadaa72d1" :answer/id #uuid "c6e8a0d8-b430-5f68-8077-a2d68a71116c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}-{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140337/selection/67b705ef58ac70e0b024907c1cb7e13926d11a26731b4d18530e5bb24d7478c7" :answer/id #uuid "af6ba6e0-b92d-5ea7-a928-a0eec364aa48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}-{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140337/selection/85fef46d11e90436ea160702e157dfb2fe9dfdeaede0a46d04deb1d9b6394b46" :answer/id #uuid "210c13e6-3768-53ce-91f3-2d63cbbc0b73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-{(x+3)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140337/selection/1581b77f5bc2e0c795660eefec20628751cb26fec5efd9ba1cb4bb6b2cd0e0bf" :answer/id #uuid "713ee8ca-4fc0-5a69-9822-b70bffbc5202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/val