dcd-5a32-9802-3c2adc6f395a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140528" :question/problem "Rewrite $2{x}^{2}-12x+16$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $2.$ So, we take out a factor of $2$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n2({x}^{2}-6x+8)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-6x+8\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+8\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${3}^{2},$ writing the constant term $8$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}}_{⏟}-{3}^{2}+8\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}-{3}^{2}+8\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}-1\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-6x+8) & =2((x-3)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =2{(x-3)}^{2}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{(x-3)}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140528/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "564f2cf7-aaaf-5dea-b619-a560c3151fcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-52522/selection/d751f545d1107e800c9b253d329982fc41416c7684867f571dd546d05dfedc1b" :answer/id #uuid "269327ae-c104-5963-9371-dcd16bcbf691" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{(x-1)}^{2}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52522/selection/4e9bc3dabe6e594d1bd7339d727b0655a63fa2c616092d9281f0de9cfb8e382a" :answer/id #uuid "ac41a758-6623-51bc-bbf9-32e2b7f66432" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x-1)}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52522/selection/64801c04e909c53fc7cec91c21d54c624698c930d568436e027a13d0418cc33b" :answer/id #uuid "68ac2a51-ea40-535d-9221-fd727b855447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{(x-1)}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52522/selection/3871189f813a6a0ebc7b1084a01e4104f8828b90fdf69db775d8890731e0fdb3" :answer/id #uuid "6b3d5733-24d5-5218-879b-144005024208" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{(x-1)}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52522/selection/912c850b9573b3471ace1b90f4b57a41a132600ee59ab9db6076019663d38886" :answer/id #uuid "bdb58b7a-f47b-5fb3-b1dc-7f3a6b14cb32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{(x+1)}^{2}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52522/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c5e41a-4418-5321-96d6-934194732f89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-52522/selection/3871189f813a6a0ebc7b1084a01e4104f8828b90fdf69db775d8890731e0fdb3" :answer-field/choices ["q-52522/selection/d751f545d1107e800c9b253d329982fc41416c7684867f571dd546d05dfedc1b" "q-52522/selection/4e9bc3dabe6e594d1bd7339d727b0655a63fa2c616092d9281f0de9cfb8e382a" "q-52522/selection/64801c04e909c53fc7cec91c21d54c624698c930d568436e027a13d0418cc33b" "q-52522/selection/3871189f813a6a0ebc7b1084a01e4104f8828b90fdf69db775d8890731e0fdb3" "q-52522/selection/912c850b9573b3471ace1b90f4b57a41a132600ee59ab9db6076019663d38886"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-52522" :question/id #uuid "3ca1d25a-a8f7-54fa-8b13-40f3f076798d" :question/math-academy-id "q-52522" :question/problem "Rewrite $2{x}^{2}-4x+3$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $2.$ So, we take out a factor of $2$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n2({x}^{2}-2x+\\frac{3}{2})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x+\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1x+\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${1}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{3}{2}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1x+{1}^{2}}_{⏟}-{1}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-2x+\\frac{3}{2}) & =2((x-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2{(x-1)}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2{(x-1)}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-52522/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "564f2cf7-aaaf-5dea-b619-a560c3151fcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-52522"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-52542"] :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-52537/selection/a84f05c05448ef393317e2c19c6fae3c9cc8d112c23b7a716fbf752f9c4b3407" :answer/id #uuid "cd40f0a6-2231-5696-affa-82b330ffa7b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52537/selection/b385c0cc3525896794a50cdc66fb782d273de5f5e168d87ec1e9ae9fd75aea12" :answer/id #uuid "ced2f86f-87d5-585f-91dd-750771cc63d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52537/selection/ff6e9b572190ac8d77dad7180d90350b41a441f22f368687e31f6d0c82199636" :answer/id #uuid "ce2e0f20-8f9c-54b7-b7d8-8b0c5bb92c72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(6x-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52537/selection/ae13a1788c9202dc884aa859f7fc5771154e15e6690d9aaa0e5e3361648a4e1c" :answer/id #uuid "93b251de-d086-5889-85c0-78704e227dd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(6x-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52537/selection/ec6535f37e24b0314a90dd71081b434cf35d895bb7b1fb8b11b9f747c1f634e4" :answer/id #uuid "af69af48-f942-50db-b93c-6dd9ceb122c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52537/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0f973b0-b05e-55c0-8cf5-ad2803007485" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-52537/selection/b385c0cc3525896794a50cdc66fb782d273de5f5e168d87ec1e9ae9fd75aea12" :answer-field/choices ["q-52537/selection/a84f05c05448ef393317e2c19c6fae3c9cc8d112c23b7a716fbf752f9c4b3407" "q-52537/selection/b385c0cc3525896794a50cdc66fb782d273de5f5e168d87ec1e9ae9fd75aea12" "q-52537/selection/ff6e9b572190ac8d77dad7180d90350b41a441f22f368687e31f6d0c82199636" "q-52537/selection/ae13a1788c9202dc884aa859f7fc5771154e15e6690d9aaa0e5e3361648a4e1c" "q-52537/selection/ec6535f37e24b0314a90dd71081b434cf35d895bb7b1fb8b11b9f747c1f634e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-52537" :question/id #uuid "1ef409a8-4695-5cd6-bd99-388a5ee00c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-52537" :question/problem "Rewrite $6{x}^{2}-2x$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $6.$ So, we take out a factor of $6$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n6({x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}x)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}x\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}:$ \n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}x+{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{36}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6({x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}x) & =6({(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{36}) \\\\  & =6{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{36} \\\\  & =6{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-52537/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "564f2cf7-aaaf-5dea-b619-a560c3151fcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-52537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-218756/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "5b5d113c-dff8-5359-848c-cb9940966738" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218756/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae5c7583-c039-5458-ba03-b70e4b9a1e39" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218756/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-218756/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218756/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6f8db0c4-b2df-52ed-bcbb-004be85083bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218756/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "145625b6-5da8-56d3-8322-61dd79fc624c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218756/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-218756/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218756/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d75548dc-64f3-5644-85b3-cb5e1b4366dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218756/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a87eb0c-e54d-5280-9178-5a5d1f34d58c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218756/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-218756/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218756" :question/id #uuid "32983a3e-5ad8-5b11-aeaa-c98688c6494d" :question/math-academy-id "q-218756" :question/problem "Rewrite $6{p}^{2}-12p+7$ by completing the square.\n\n$6{p}^{2}-12p+7=$\n{{field-1}}\n$(p\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$)^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $6.$ So, we take out a factor of $6$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n6({p}^{2}-2p+\\frac{7}{6})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{p}^{2}-2p+\\frac{7}{6}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{p}^{2}-2\\cdot 1p+\\frac{7}{6}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${1}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{7}{6}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{p}^{2}-2\\cdot 1p+{1}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{1}^{2}+\\frac{7}{6}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(p-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}+\\frac{7}{6}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(p-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6({p}^{2}-2p+\\frac{7}{6}) & =6({(p-1)}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =6{(p-1)}^{2}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =6{(p-1)}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-218756/field-1" "q-218756/field-2" "q-218756/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "564f2cf7-aaaf-5dea-b619-a560c3151fcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-218756"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-218759/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "a4e6011f-cde4-5353-9da0-341cc54d9bbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218759/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe4a4169-68ed-5c6a-940c-4132a6cbf957" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218759/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-218759/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218759/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c6fa2de9-c2ee-575d-a2f7-deeccb26e1bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218759/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "270a4a97-0cb4-517b-9dd9-d5c509cd8c62" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218759/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-218759/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218759/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2498ec73-64e6-5612-82d3-a184cc200dac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218759/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "880f07a1-8260-5d8f-812c-bd45ba637d62" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218759/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-218759/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218759" :question/id #uuid "9d1b8685-4e2a-5ec9-b1ad-83d2f5c1d7b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-218759" :question/problem "Rewrite $-8{x}^{2}+32x-29$ by completing the square.\n\n$-8{x}^{2}+32x-29=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$)^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-8.$ So, we take out a factor of $-8$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-8({x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{29}{8})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{29}{8}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+\\frac{29}{8}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${2}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{29}{8}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{2}^{2}-\\frac{29}{8}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}-\\frac{29}{8}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}-\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8({x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{29}{8}) & =-8({(x-2)}^{2}-\\frac{3}{8}) \\\\  & =-8{(x-2)}^{2}+(-8)\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{8}) \\\\  & =-8{(x-2)}^{2}+3 \\\\  & =3-8{(x-2)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-218759/field-1" "q-218759/field-2" "q-218759/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3202d7cc-541b-553b-8ec1-d4ea85dd0590"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-218759"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35079/selection/ef20f11a5830f69f42c6d53539992b9f6180f5245586724bd15854bf7afac021" :answer/id #uuid "b9fb4ff9-5d57-5854-9c61-39b0c95c4607" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{(z-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{49}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35079/selection/8ba5f28a10f8e6b05f0a6fb8e61fde2f260cc46abe8ffc7fe5089e0a2d6061d8" :answer/id #uuid "3057a71a-0f0d-50c4-8eda-2d5828333d0a" :answe